stratfor nathan district council is  currently consulting on a site  allocations plan  this video outlines four specific site  proposals put forward in the site  allocations plan in various locations  across stafford navy district  the first one is proposal rural one  former knapton brickworks  the site is located just to the west of  napton on the hill and about two and a  half miles east of southern  it is a brownfield site so the principle  of redevelopment is supported  various planning permissions have been  granted in the past most recently for a  complex of live work units but none have  been implemented  the plan proposes a development of up to  80 dwellings public open space  and a nature reserve development at the  site would remove the current eyesore  and contamination  and control anti-social activities as  well as manage the existing habitats  however it will be important to improve  the relationship between the site and  knapton village  including for pedestrians and cyclists  and take into account the impact of  adjacent adjust industrial uses  an outline planning application for the  site was submitted in november 2018  but it is not yet determined due to the  range of complex issues that need to be  resolved  then we have proposal world 2 university  of warwick wells born campus  this is an extensive site situated to  the north of wells born but with a large  part lying in charcot parish  the site has a long history of research  relating to agriculture  the university is developing a long-term  strategy for the site  a new innovation campus is proposed to  support research and development in a  range of specialist sectors such as life  science  automotive and medical  three specific areas have been  identified for development within the  site  as shown on the map by the hatching  land to the north west of the existing  buildings land to the south  east of the existing buildings and land  fronting salford road for commercialed  stratford road sorry for commercial uses  to help facilitate investment on the  campus itself  the scale and extent of development on  the site will require thorough  assessment due to the range of sensitive  issues involved these include the  proximity of charcot conservation area  and the registered childcare park as  well as the existing trees and hedgerows  then there's proposal rule 3 quintin  rail technology centre near  long marston the plan proposes the  development of a rail-based innovation  and technology facility on this site  it is located several miles to the  southwest of stratford-upon-avon  on part of the former long-marks and  storage depot  it is adjacent to the former  stratford-upon-avon to honeybourne  railway and next to the new community  being established at the unveil  the site provides the uk's only looped  rail test track  and it's only specifically built light  rail test facility  as such the district council considers  it is appropriate to safeguard the rail  related activities on the site  however the council acknowledges that  business needs change over time  and that the site covers a large area as  such it will also support enabling  development that helps secure the  long-term future of rail activities on  the site  the scale and extent of additional  development on the site will need to  take into account matters relating to  flood risk ecology  and trafficked impact  and then finally there's proposal world  war 5 long marston airfield  the core strategy identifies long  marston airfield as a new settlement for  3  500 homes phase one comprising 400 homes  and a local centre  has planning consent and is already  underway  it is acknowledged that there is a major  constraint on the highway network in  stratford-upon-avon particularly south  of the river  however a recent transport assessment  confirms that there is some additional  capacity to enable further development  at the south of the town  before the southwestern relief road is  constructed  the district council considers that most  of this spare capacity should be taken  up by long mars in airfield  since the site is an existing allocation  in the core strategy  the boundary for the long mars in  airfield new settlement is indicated as  a dashed line on the map  the extent of this specific proposal is  shown by a solid line and marked a  it is important to ensure that  development of the new settlement  continues to come forward in accordance  with the approved master plan  and that the necessary infrastructure is  provided alongside new homes  consequently proposal world five seeks  to provide clarity  regarding the next phase of the  development this includes land for  primary school  employment and for open space  i hope you found this useful remember  you can find out more in the site  allocations plan  and submit any comments you have by  visiting our website at  www.stratford.gov  dot uk forward slash zappo
 

